## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP over partitioning with a non-trivial segment value (max letter value).

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions with exact k segments
- Precomputing segment values (maxChar)
- Reconstructing the cut points

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPartitionValue(s, k){
  const n = s.length;
  const val = [...s].map(c => c.charCodeAt(0) - 96); // a=1..z=26
  const maxChar = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(n+1).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    let m=0;
    for(let j=i;j<n;j++){
      m = Math.max(m, val[j]);
      maxChar[i][j+1] = m;
    }
  }
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const pre = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const cand = dp[p][t-1] + maxChar[p][i];
        if(cand > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = cand; pre[i][t] = p; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return {value: dp[n][k], cuts: []};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle k=1 or k=n in constant time?
- Can you reduce space to O(nk) without losing reconstruction capabilities?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP on partitioning with a minimax objective, a practical budgeting scenario.

## Key Concepts
- DP over partitions; - Recurrence: min over j of max of subproblem and block sum; - Reconstruction via parent pointers.

## Code Example
```javascript
// sketch
function partitionMinMaxSum(a, k) {
  const n = a.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) pref[i+1]=pref[i]+a[i];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n},()=>new Array(k+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n},()=>new Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][1]=pref[i+1];
  for (let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for (let i=0;i<n;i++){
      for (let j=0;j<i;j++){
        const val = Math.max(dp[j][t-1], pref[i+1]-pref[j+0]);
        if (val<dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; par[i][t]=j; }
      }
    }
  }
  return {best: dp[n-1][Math.min(k,n)], cuts: par};
}
```

